  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Outcome</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expanded power sector services and stable power supplies in Kabul</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Additional 55,000 grid connected households in south west Kabul by 2016(baseline: 0) 
Progress/Status: On Sep 2013 the Contract for power distribution network for 40,000 household connections was awarded to FEKA Construction Industry and Trade Inc, Engineering works and surveys commenced in March 2014. Supply of materials and equipment started in September 2014 and installation works started from November 2014 and the contract completed in May 2017. 
Data Source: ICE quarterly report
DABS annual report 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="0" year="2009"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2016-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2016-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="55000"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Grid in south west Kabul Darchi-e-Bashi area expanded by 400 km by 2016 (baseline:  40 km in 2007) 
Progress/Status: The contract for grid expansion in South West Kabul (Darchi-e-Barchi and Arghandi) was awarded to FEKA Construction Industry and Trade Inc. The physcial work was completed in June 2017 and package has been closed. The scope of work for distribution network includes design, supply, installation, testing, commissioning, documentation and startup of the new medium and low voltage distribution network to provide a reliable distribution network to the 40,000 household in proposed areas. 
Data Source: ICE quarterly report
DABS annual report 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="40" year="2009"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2016-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2016-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="400"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Power system capable to supply 1,450 megawatts (MW) of connected load by 2017 from North East Power System (NEPS) from 400MW in 2010 
Progress/Status: Various donors along with ADB are implementing respective programs to extend NEPS&amp;apos; capacity and strengthen institutional arrangements for Operations and Management (O&amp;M) of power infrastructure in Afghanistan. The physical work of 600 km of 500kv power transmission line connecting the TKM to AFG grind is under construction starting from TKM border till Kabul with expected completion by 2021. 
Data Source: DABS annual report
DABS and AEIC websites
ICE quarterly report 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="400" year="2009"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2016-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2016-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="1450"></target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
