    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Transmission coverage expanded from Chimtala to South West Kabul 
Indicator: New Kabul Southwest substation (220/110 kV) by 2016 
Progress/Status: The originally proposed location of the sub-station could have a significant resettlement impact therefore a new site (9 kms south from the original location) was proposed and approved. ADB approved awarding an EPC contract for construction of 220/20kV Arghundi substation to Siemens Pakistan. The physical work has been completed and completion certificate has been submitted to ADB on 15 January 2019. DABS is processing the final payment within winding period on 30 Sep 2019. DABS and MOF has covered the shortfall of the contract. 
Data Source: ICE quarterly report
DABS annual report 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
